  "methodology_other": "Dataset: Administrative boundaries acquired from the Qatar planning and statistics authority.\n\nP-codes developed by OCHA",
  "name": "cod-ab-qat",
  "notes": "Qatar administrative level 0-3 boundaries (COD-AB) dataset version 02.  \n  \nThis dataset is structured into 3 levels:  \n- Admin 1: 8 Municipality  \n- Admin 2: 87 Zone, partial coverage  \n- Admin 3: 718 District, partial coverage  \n  \n  \nDates associated with this dataset:  \n- 30 April 2024: dataset reviewed for accuracy and completeness  \n- 27 June 2024: valid for use by the humanitarian community  \n- 30 November 2015: last edit to the dataset before publishing  \n- 30 November 2015: boundaries created by the source  \n  \nContributed by [OCHA Middle East and North Africa (ROMENA)](https://data.humdata.org/organization/ocha-romena).  \nQuality assured, configured, and published by [OCHA Field Information Services (FIS)](https://data.humdata.org/organization/ocha-fiss) and [HDX](https://data.humdata.org/organization/hdx).  \n  \nPart of the dataset: [Global Subnational Administrative Boundaries](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-global)",
